        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Try queuing an asynchronous I/O write operation. If the file is NOT open and ready to be operated on, returns immediately. Else, queues a new I/O operation, increments the pending I/O operation reference counter, then calls <ref refid="structMemoryInFiles_1_1Impl_1_1FileInfo_1a3c4f9dcf53259cf84204553bd070c777" kindref="member">FileInfo::TryStartNextQueuedIoOperation()</ref> to trigger processing of the next queued I/O operation. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>memoryBlockInfoRef</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The associated memory block. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>offsetWithinFile</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The file offset to begin writing to. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type-erased input begin pointer to read from. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>length</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The data length in bytes to write. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>handlerPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type-erased I/O completion handler pointer. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>True if the file is open and ready to be operated on, or False otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="post"><para>MIGHT increment the pending I/O operation reference counter (m_queuedOperationsReferenceCount). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
