          <type><ref refid="structMemoryInFiles_1_1Impl_1_1io__operation__t" kindref="compound">io_operation_t</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>op</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Finalize completion of the given I/O operation. If the associated memory block is due deletion and there are no pending I/O operations left, initiates an asynchronous request to <ref refid="structMemoryInFiles_1_1Impl_1a42103be7fc11d1ab58cb2d6b6769b2cc" kindref="member">Impl::ForceDeleteMemoryBlock()</ref> to clean up the memory block. Calls <ref refid="structMemoryInFiles_1_1Impl_1_1FileInfo_1a3c4f9dcf53259cf84204553bd070c777" kindref="member">FileInfo::TryStartNextQueuedIoOperation()</ref> to trigger processing of the next queued I/O operation. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>op</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The completed I/O operation. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="post"><para>Decrements the pending I/O operation reference counter (m_queuedOperationsReferenceCount). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
